இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with chest"},{"surface":"வையகம்","parts":[{"text":"வையகம்","lemma":"வையகம்","gloss":"world"}],"gloss":"world"},{"surface":"விளக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"விளக்கும்","lemma":"விளக்குதல்","gloss":"illuminating"}],"gloss":"illuminating"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விரவுமணி","parts":[{"text":"விரவு","lemma":"விரவுதல்","gloss":"mixed"},{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"gems"}],"gloss":"mixed gems"},{"surface":"ஒளிர்வரும்","parts":[{"text":"ஒளிர்","lemma":"ஒளிர்தல்","gloss":"shining"},{"text":"வரும்","lemma":"வருதல்","gloss":"coming"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"அரவுஉறழ்","parts":[{"text":"அரவு","lemma":"அரவு","gloss":"snake"},{"text":"உறழ்","lemma":"உறழ்தல்","gloss":"resembling"}],"gloss":"snake-resembling"},{"surface":"ஆரமொடு","parts":[{"text":"ஆரம்","lemma":"ஆரம்","gloss":"necklace"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"ஒடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with necklace"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புரையோன்","parts":[{"text":"புரை","lemma":"புரை","gloss":"noble"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ஓன்","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"noble one"},{"surface":"மேனி","parts":[{"text":"மேனி","lemma":"மேனி","gloss":"body"}],"gloss":"body"},{"surface":"பூந்துகில்","parts":[{"text":"பூந்துகில்","lemma":"பூந்துகில்","gloss":"flower-like fine cloth"}],"gloss":"flower-like fine cloth","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கலிங்கம்","parts":[{"text":"கலிங்கம்","lemma":"கலிங்கம்","gloss":"garment"}],"gloss":"garment"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உரை","parts":[{"text":"உரை","lemma":"உரை","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"},{"surface":"செல","parts":[{"text":"செல","lemma":"செல்லுதல்","gloss":"to spread"}],"gloss":"to spread"},{"surface":"அருளியோனே","parts":[{"text":"அருளி","lemma":"அருளுதல்","gloss":"graciously giving"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ஓன்","gloss":"he"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"he who graciously gave"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பறை","parts":[{"text":"பறை","lemma":"பறை","gloss":"drum"}],"gloss":"drum"},{"surface":"இசை","parts":[{"text":"இசை","lemma":"இசை","gloss":"sound"}],"gloss":"sound"},{"surface":"அருவி","parts":[{"text":"அருவி","lemma":"அருவி","gloss":"waterfall"}],"gloss":"waterfall"},{"surface":"பாயல்","parts":[{"text":"பாயல்","lemma":"பாயல்","gloss":"Pāyal hill"}],"gloss":"Pāyal hill"},{"surface":"கோவே","parts":[{"text":"கோ","lemma":"கோ","gloss":"king"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"vocative"}],"gloss":"O King!"}]}],"literal":"As the moon's light hid and the morning star rose / In the well-made excellent house ... / The spotted-feathered rooster, knowing the time, crowed / As the flower buds in the pond blossomed, the bards / With small lutes, skillful in hand, played knowing their duty / At the sweet dawn that followed the night / Where suppliants gather without limit under the fragrant canopy / In order of merit, Vañcaṉ of truthful words stayed / Unless friends approach, for enemies / Like a stone cave where a pack of tigers sleeps / The ancient town of great fame is impossible to enter / Like the moon, my clear-voiced taṭāri drum / Beating it as the long leather straps of night-talk vibrated / O you who fills the receiving vessels of those who come thinking of you! / 'May you remain in an unfailing state for us,' saying thus / Making my arrival known / Rejoicing greatly for a small thing / With a loving face, removing from my waist / The ragged clothes with straw attached, and on my waist / Making me wear a fine shining cloth like spreading smoke / In a rare-to-get bowl that shone like emitting fire / Pouring clear liquor in which one's reflection is seen, to the brim / Not only granting me to drink, but also the fried venison curry / Cut from the meat, which he himself ate from the bowl / And straightened rice like heron's claws, for my kinsfolk to eat and be satisfied / With a mountain-like chest that illuminates the world / With a snake-like necklace of shining mixed gems / The noble one, the flower-patterned fine garment for his body / He graciously granted, so that his fame spreads / The king of Pāyal hill with waterfalls sounding like drums!","translation":"As the moonlight faded and the morning star rose, the roosters crowed at dawn and the pond lilies bloomed. Bards played their small lutes with practiced skill. Under a fragrant canopy, the truthful king Vañcaṉ received bards in order of merit. His ancient, famous town is as impenetrable to enemies as a cave where tigers sleep, welcoming only friends. I arrived there, beating my moon-like taṭāri drum with its long leather straps, and blessed him, saying, 'May you always remain in this unfailing state of generosity!' He rejoiced greatly at my humble arrival. With a warm, smiling face, he removed my straw-ridden rags and dressed me in fine silk as light as spreading smoke. He poured clear, reflective liquor to the brim of a glowing bowl, and fed my kinsfolk with choice fried venison and white rice as delicate as heron's claws. Finally, this noble king of Pāyal hill, whose chest is adorned with a snake-like necklace of brilliant gems, gifted me his own fine royal garments so that his fame might spread far and wide.","modern":"நிலவொளி மறைய, விடிவெள்ளி தோன்றியது. சிறந்த இல்லத்தில் சேவல்கள் பொழுது அறிந்து கூவின. பொய்கையில் தாமரை மொட்டுகள் மலர்ந்தன. பாணர்கள் யாழ்களை முறைப்படி வாசித்தனர். விடியற்காலையில், கொடையாளியான வஞ்சனின் அரண்மனைப் பந்தலில் பரிசிலர் வரிசையாகக் கூடினர். நண்பர்கள் மட்டுமே நுழையக்கூடிய, பகைவர்களுக்குப் புலி குகை போன்ற அச்சம் தரும் மூதூரில் வாழும் வஞ்சனிடம் சென்றேன். என் வட்டவடிவத் தடாரிப் பறையை முழக்கி, 'எம்மைப் பாதுகாக்கும் நீ என்றும் வாழ்க!' என்று என் வருகையை அறிவித்தேன். அவன் என் எளிய வருகைக்காகப் பெரிதும் மகிழ்ந்து, இன்முகத்துடன் வரவேற்றான். என் இடையில் இருந்த கிழிந்த ஆடையை நீக்கி, புகை போன்ற மெல்லிய ஆடையை உடுத்தச் செய்தான். நெருப்புப் போல ஒளிரும் கிண்ணத்தில் தெளிந்த மதுவை ஊற்றித் தந்தான். தான் உண்ட கிண்ணத்தில் இருந்த மான் கறி வறுவலையும், கொக்கின் நகம் போன்ற வெண்மையான சோற்றையும் என் சுற்றத்தார் வயிறார உண்ணச் செய்தான். உலகமே போற்றும் மார்பையும், நாகம் போன்ற ஒளிவீசும் ஆரத்தையும் உடைய அந்த வள்ளல், தன் மேனியில் அணிந்திருந்த சிறந்த பட்டாடையையும் எனக்குப் பரிசாக அளித்தான். அவனே அருவிகள் முழங்கும் பாயல் மலையின் தலைவன் ஆவான்.","explanation":"In this Pāṭāṇ poem, the poet Tiruttāmaṉār praises the extraordinary generosity of the Chera chieftain Vañcaṉ of Pāyal hill. Arriving at dawn, the poet plays his taṭāri drum and blesses the king, who welcomes him with immense joy despite the poet's humble status. The king immediately replaces the poet's straw-ridden rags with fine, smoke-like garments and serves him premium liquor in a glowing vessel. Furthermore, the king feeds the poet's entire family with choice venison and fine white rice, and even gifts his own royal silk garments and ornaments. The poem beautifully contrasts the king's terrifying, tiger-cave-like fortress for enemies with his warm, boundless hospitality toward bards and friends.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}